🇺🇸 American tech billionaire and co-owner of Palantir Alex Karp has bought himself a 15,000 hectare property in northern Sweden for €25M.

His newly founded Swedish company Cladonia describes itself as engaged in forestry and denies any plans for data centers. The property is almost the size of the City of Stockholm and is located in the middle of nowhere.

